description:
Design a Pulse Width Modulation (PWM) generator. The circuit takes an 8-bit control input representing the duty cycle, allowing for variable control of the PWM signal's width. The PWM output signal is high when the current count, which increments on each clock cycle, is less than a calculated threshold based on the duty cycle. The counter resets upon reaching a maximum value (255). This implementation is useful for applications requiring variable signal control, such as motor speed regulation or LED brightness adjustment.
