Design a combinational logic circuit that takes a 5-bit input and produces a 5-bit output based on specific logical conditions applied to the individual bits of the input. The output is generated using various logical operations (AND, OR, XOR, NOT) to implement a set of predefined logic functions. The output L is formed by calculating five different signals (L40, L31, L22, L13, L04), which encapsulate conditions based on the input bits, representing encoded output values derived from the combinations of the input bits.
